-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  dir_exeicon_err_decode.pcpp - Directive: an icon file that holds no image

  Break step of dir_exeicon and dir_exeicon_linux: the file exists (this very
  file) but holds no image. The compiler decodes the icon before the build
  on every target (on Linux to build it in, on Windows before the exe is
  stamped), so the mistake is the same report at the same place on both, and
  nothing is built (the report names the file and the decoder's reason).
*******************************************************************************/

module exe dir_exeicon_err_decode;

/*
  @@test
    kind error
  @@end
*/

@exeicon "$P:res/tests/dir/dir_exeicon_err_decode.pcpp"; // ERROR CMP0008@10: cannot build the icon

begin
end.
